Today I am turning thirty-two years old.
I arrive at the office and go into the break room.
My team lead Katrin and my colleague Sven are waiting for me there.
There is a cake on the table.
Next to it is fresh coffee.
"Happy Birthday, Maya!" they call out together.
I am genuinely touched.
"I had absolutely no idea!" I say.
Sven laughs and gives me a piece of cake.
We drink our coffee and eat together.
The cake is fantastic.
"Thank you very much for this wonderful morning," I say.
"You have organized this wonderfully."
Katrin smiles.
"We very gladly did this," she says.
"The cake was a very good idea," I add.
"That was Sven's idea," Katrin answers.
"He bought the cake this morning."
My birthday has started perfectly.
